<%- include('partials/head') %>
<section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap">
  <p class="eyebrow">Revenue-Based Financing</p>
  <h1>Upfront capital, repaid as your business earns.</h1>
  <p class="lead">Revenue-based financing gives you $5,000 to $300,000 now in exchange for a fixed amount of your future receivables, collected through small automatic payments.</p>
  <a href="/apply" class="btn btn-green btn-lg">Apply for RBF</a>
</div></section>

<section class="sec"><div class="wrap split">
  <div>
    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <p>You receive a lump sum upfront. In return, a fixed total amount is repaid through auto-debited daily or weekly payments from your business account. Because payments are tied to revenue, they can fluctuate with your sales.</p>
    <p>The total payment is set at signing. If repayment takes longer than expected during a slower stretch, the total you owe doesn't change.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="spec">
    <div><span>Funding amount</span><strong>$5,000 – $300,000</strong></div>
    <div><span>Estimated payment period</span><strong>3 – 12 months</strong></div>
    <div><span>Payment frequency</span><strong>Daily or weekly</strong></div>
    <div><span>Payment method</span><strong>Automatic debit</strong></div>
    <div><span>Total cost</span><strong>Fixed at signing</strong></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="sec sec-alt"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="sec-head"><h2>Is RBF a good fit?</h2></div>
  <div class="cards cards-2">
    <article class="card plain"><h3>Usually a great fit if you…</h3><ul class="checks">
      <li>Have steady deposits into a business bank account</li>
      <li>Need capital faster than a bank can provide it</li>
      <li>Have seasonal or uneven revenue</li>
      <li>Want a fixed cost you can plan around</li>
    </ul></article>
    <article class="card plain"><h3>Good to know</h3><ul class="dots">
      <li>RBF is a purchase of future receivables, not a traditional loan.</li>
      <li>Cost depends on your revenue, time in business, credit profile and term.</li>
      <li>Your advisor will show the total payback before you sign anything.</li>
    </ul></article>
  </div>
</div></section>
<%- include('partials/foot') %>
